codex
The source implementation matches the canonical algorithm on ordinary ASCII inputs, but the contract is Python-string based and the shortcut has a Unicode-sensitive risk: `str.swapcase()` can change some non-letters when another character makes the `any(isalpha)` branch true. I’m making that boundary explicit in an independent differential harness instead of assuming the ASCII examples define the entire domain.
